Captain B.K. Tyagi Becomes INSA President!
Marine Tanks 

New Delhi, September 24. At the 46th Annual General Meeting of the Indian National Shipowners’ Association (INSA), Captain B.K. Tyagi, Chairman and Managing Director of the Shipping Corporation of India (SCI), was elected President for the year 2026-27.

Captain Tyagi has more than three decades of experience in the maritime sector. He began his career as a maritime officer with SCI and has handled responsibilities in various areas, including shipping, chartering, marine HR, training and offshore operations. He has been serving as the Chairman and Managing Director of SCI since September 2022.

Established in 1929, #INSA is the leading representative organisation of shipowners and #shipping companies in India. The organisation raises issues related to shipping policy, industry regulations, maritime business and seafarers’ welfare before the government and various forums.

